window.docContents[25].resolve({"/UD-IV___-abstraction/Parameters-by-reference/#Core-C______--UD-IV___-abstraction--Parameters-by-reference":{"contents":"A parameter  receives the location of its argument, which must denote a location of exactly the type . The binding of  in the function environment is an alias, as the local reference of UD III, and the return does not free it. In  the parameter has the type of its referent.Two reference parameters bound to the same argument alias each other, and a write through one is read through the other, as in C++.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009UD IV, abstraction","header":"5.2. Parameters by reference","id":"/UD-IV___-abstraction/Parameters-by-reference/#Core-C______--UD-IV___-abstraction--Parameters-by-reference"}});